From f6fe7c81c40939ea91af2a21a590b540cb329ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(allwinner): offer CPU_SUSPEND natively on the H616

The H616 has no SCP, so the native PSCI ops offer no CPU_SUSPEND and
Linux has no idle state beyond WFI.

Add SUNXI_NATIVE_CPU_SUSPEND: core-level CPU_SUSPEND through the
CPUIDLE block that CPU_OFF already uses. The block changes the reset
and gating registers itself, so CPU_ON must not read-modify-write them:
at setup each secondary core is powered up once to a stub that leaves
it to the block, and CPU_ON then sets the core's wake bit and sends it
an SGI. All cores are set to AArch64 once at setup, so a power-cycled
core 0 does not restart in the BROM.

Backport of the version under upstream review to lts-v2.14.11.

Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/56325
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
